    "body": "I found that encryption relied on the cipher-provided IV, while decryption reads the 12-byte IV from the framed input. Dynamic analysis did not observe the IV material as coming from a randomized source, which violates the tool’s `GCMParameterSpecSpec` usage rule.\n\nI now generate a random 12-byte IV for each encryption, initialize AES-GCM with the existing 128-bit tag parameters, and create a new `Cipher` for every operation. Decryption continues to use the IV carried in its input. This is safe because the public entry points, exception behavior, and `[12-byte IV || encrypted payload]` format remain unchanged.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`:amethyst:assembleFdroidDebug`).\n\nAI assistance was used for this contribution.\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
